;; The modules _multiprocessing and _posixshmem (queue 231; Modules/_multiprocessing/semaphore.c, multiprocessing.c and
;; posixshmem.c): SemLock ported method by method over POSIX named semaphores, and those over Go as musl makes them. A
;; semaphore is musl's: the file /dev/shm/NAME (__shm_mapname's name rules), a sem_t of 32 bytes mapped shared, its value
;; the first int; a process opens a name once (sem_open's table: the same mapping, counted). What C does with atomics
;; on the mapping is done here under a lock, as Go forms have no atomic operation on a mapping's memory: flock(2) on the
;; file (between processes) and a mutex (between this process's threads, which share the file's description); the
;; second int counts the waiters, which sleep in futex(2) on the value's address (reflect's Pointer of the mapping, as
;; mmap's msync takes it) and are woken by sem_post. A waiter on the main thread sleeps in slices of 20 ms and runs the
;; pending signals' handlers between them, as semaphore.c's sem_timedwait_save does: Go restarts futex after its own
;; signal handlers, so no EINTR reaches it.

